{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "b6f1f0c2-8d4e-4a7b-9c1e-2f3a4b5c6d7e",
		"name": "Gradely API",
		"description": "Collection for the Gradely backend API.\n\n## Setup\n1. Start the API with `pnpm run dev` (default `http://localhost:5000`).\n2. Seed the admin account with `pnpm run db:seed`. This reads `ADMIN_NAME`, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` from `.env`.\n3. Import this collection into Postman.\n4. Run **Auth → Register Student** first. The test script stores `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, `studentId`, and `studentEmail` automatically.\n5. Run **Submissions → Create Submission**. The test script stores `submissionId` for the follow-up requests.\n6. For admin requests (**List All Submissions**, **Review Submission**, **Delete User**), run **Auth → Login Admin** using the seeded admin credentials.\n\n## Endpoints covered\n- **Health**: `GET /health`\n- **Auth**: register, login, change password\n- **Users**: get/update the current profile, admin delete user\n- **Submissions**: create, list mine, admin list all, get, update, review, delete\n\n## Variables\nAll variables are collection variables, so no environment file is required. Open the collection's **Variables** tab to edit `baseUrl`, `adminEmail`, or `adminPassword`.\n\n## Authentication cookies\nRegister and Login also set httpOnly `accessToken` / `refreshToken` cookies, and the API prefers the cookie over the `Authorization: Bearer` header. Postman keeps those cookies between requests, so after switching identities (for example, **Login Admin** after **Register Student**) the admin cookie overrides the student Bearer token. If a request unexpectedly returns `403`, clear the cookies for `localhost` (Postman → Cookies, or the cookie icon next to **Send**) and retry.\n\n## Status rules\n- Students can create submissions and manage only their own while `PENDING`.\n- Admins can list all submissions, review them, and delete any submission or user.\n- A rejected submission requires `feedback`.\n- Reviewed submissions cannot be updated or reviewed again.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [
			{
				"key": "token",
				"value": "{{accessToken}}",
				"type": "string"
			}
		]
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Health",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Health Check",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["health"]
						},
						"description": "Returns the API health status. No authentication required."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"pm.test(\"API is healthy\", () => {",
									"  const json = pm.response.json();",
									"  pm.expect(json.data.status).to.eql(\"healthy\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "noauth"
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Auth",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Register Student",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Student User\",\n  \"email\": \"{{studentEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{studentPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "register"]
						},
						"description": "Registers a student. Generates a unique student email on every run and saves the returned tokens."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "prerequest",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const stamp = Date.now();",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"studentEmail\", `student-${stamp}@example.com`);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"studentPassword\", \"Password123!\");"
								]
							}
						},
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Returns user and tokens\", () => {",
									"  pm.expect(json.data.user.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"studentEmail\"));",
									"  pm.expect(json.data.tokens.accessToken).to.be.a(\"string\");",
									"});",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", json.data.tokens.accessToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", json.data.tokens.refreshToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"studentId\", json.data.user.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "noauth"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Login Student",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{studentEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{studentPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
						},
						"description": "Logs in the student created by Register Student and refreshes the stored access token."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", json.data.tokens.accessToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", json.data.tokens.refreshToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"studentId\", json.data.user.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "noauth"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Change Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "PATCH",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"oldPassword\": \"{{studentPassword}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"{{nextStudentPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "change-password"]
						},
						"description": "Changes the authenticated user's password. Run **Login Student** (or **Register Student**) first so `studentPassword` holds the current password and the cookie jar still holds the student session; run it before **Login Admin**. `newPassword` must be 8-128 characters with an uppercase letter, a lowercase letter, a number, and a special character, without spaces, and must differ from `oldPassword`. The pre-request script generates a fresh password and the test script saves it to `studentPassword`, so reruns keep working. Existing tokens are not revoked."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "prerequest",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"nextStudentPassword\", `Password${Date.now()}!`);"
								]
							}
						},
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Password was changed\", () => pm.expect(json.data).to.eql(null));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"studentPassword\", pm.collectionVariables.get(\"nextStudentPassword\"));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Login Admin",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
						},
						"description": "Logs in the seeded admin and stores `adminAccessToken`. Run `pnpm run db:seed` first; it creates the admin from `ADMIN_NAME`, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in `.env`. The defaults below match the values added to `.env`. This also sets admin auth cookies, which take precedence over Bearer tokens; clear the `localhost` cookies before running student requests again."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"User is an admin\", () => pm.expect(json.data.user.role).to.eql(\"ADMIN\"));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminAccessToken\", json.data.tokens.accessToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminId\", json.data.user.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "noauth"
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Users",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get My Profile",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "users", "me"]
						},
						"description": "Returns the authenticated user's profile without the password: `id`, `name`, `email`, `role`, `status`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Returns the current user\", () => pm.expect(json.data.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"studentId\")));",
									"pm.test(\"Password is not exposed\", () => pm.expect(json.data).to.not.have.property(\"password\"));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Update My Profile",
					"request": {
						"method": "PATCH",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Student User Updated\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "users", "me"]
						},
						"description": "Updates the authenticated user's `name` and/or `email`. At least one field is required; `email` must be unique and valid. If you change the email, update `studentEmail` so **Login Student** keeps working."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Name was updated\", () => pm.expect(json.data.name).to.include(\"Updated\"));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Delete User (Admin)",
					"request": {
						"method": "DELETE",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{targetUserId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "users", "{{targetUserId}}"]
						},
						"description": "Admin-only. Permanently deletes the user whose id is stored in `targetUserId` (copy the id from `studentId` or from any admin list response). Their submissions are cascade-deleted. Run **Login Admin** first, and set `targetUserId` to a throwaway account rather than the student used by the rest of the collection."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Deleted user is returned\", () => pm.expect(json.data.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"targetUserId\")));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.unset(\"targetUserId\");"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "bearer",
						"bearer": [
							{
								"key": "token",
								"value": "{{adminAccessToken}}",
								"type": "string"
							}
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Submissions",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Create Submission",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"projectName\": \"My Portfolio Website\",\n  \"repoUrl\": \"https://github.com/student/portfolio-{{$guid}}\",\n  \"liveLink\": \"https://my-portfolio.example.com\",\n  \"description\": \"A portfolio website built with Next.js and Tailwind CSS.\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/submissions",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "submissions"]
						},
						"description": "Creates a submission for the authenticated student. `repoUrl` must be unique across all submissions and `projectName` must be unique per student; the generated GUID keeps reruns working. `projectName` is 3-255 characters, `description` is 10-5000 characters, and `repoUrl` / `liveLink` must be http(s) URLs. This endpoint is student-only. The response includes the `student` summary."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Submission is pending\", () => pm.expect(json.data.status).to.eql(\"PENDING\"));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"submissionId\", json.data.id);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"studentId\", json.data.studentId);"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "List My Submissions",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/submissions/me?page=1&limit=10",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "submissions", "me"],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "page",
									"value": "1",
									"description": "Page number (1-based)."
								},
								{
									"key": "limit",
									"value": "10",
									"description": "Items per page (1-100)."
								},
								{
									"key": "status",
									"value": "PENDING",
									"description": "Optional: PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED.",
									"disabled": true
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "Lists only the authenticated user's submissions, newest first. Restricted to the `STUDENT` and `ADMIN` roles; an admin sees only submissions they created themselves (usually none), so use **List All Submissions** for the admin view. Supports `page` (1-based), `limit` (1-100), and an optional `status` filter."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Response is paginated\", () => {",
									"  pm.expect(json.meta).to.include.keys(\"page\", \"limit\", \"total\", \"totalPages\");",
									"  pm.expect(json.data).to.be.an(\"array\");",
									"});",
									"pm.test(\"Only returns the current user's submissions\", () => {",
									"  const studentId = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"studentId\");",
									"  json.data.forEach((item) => pm.expect(item.studentId).to.eql(studentId));",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "List All Submissions (Admin)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/submissions?page=1&limit=10",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "submissions"],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "page",
									"value": "1"
								},
								{
									"key": "limit",
									"value": "10"
								},
								{
									"key": "status",
									"value": "PENDING",
									"disabled": true
								},
								{
									"key": "studentId",
									"value": "{{studentId}}",
									"disabled": true
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "Admin view of all submissions, newest first. Requires **Login Admin**. Supports `page` (1-based), `limit` (1-100), optional `status` (`PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`), and optional `studentId`. Each item includes `student` and `reviewer` summaries."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Response is paginated\", () => pm.expect(json.meta).to.include.keys(\"total\"));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "bearer",
						"bearer": [
							{
								"key": "token",
								"value": "{{adminAccessToken}}",
								"type": "string"
							}
						]
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Submission",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/submissions/{{submissionId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "submissions", "{{submissionId}}"]
						},
						"description": "Returns one submission with student and reviewer summaries. The owner or an admin may access it."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Returns the requested submission\", () => pm.expect(json.data.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"submissionId\")));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Update Submission",
					"request": {
						"method": "PATCH",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"projectName\": \"My Portfolio Website\",\n  \"description\": \"Updated description for my portfolio submission.\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/submissions/{{submissionId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "submissions", "{{submissionId}}"]
						},
						"description": "Updates editable fields (`projectName`, `repoUrl`, `liveLink`, `description`) on your own submission. Only the owner may update it, only while it is `PENDING`, and at least one field is required. `repoUrl` must stay globally unique and `projectName` unique per student. Validation matches **Create Submission**."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Description was updated\", () => pm.expect(json.data.description).to.include(\"Updated\"));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Review Submission (Admin)",
					"request": {
						"method": "PATCH",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n  \"feedback\": \"Great work. The project is approved.\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/submissions/{{submissionId}}/review",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "v1", "submissions", "{{submissionId}}", "review"]
						},
						"description": "Admin-only review of a submission. Only `PENDING` submissions can be reviewed, and a submission cannot be reviewed twice. Set `status` to `APPROVED` or `REJECTED`; rejection requires `feedback` (3-2000 characters). The response stores `reviewerId` and `reviewedAt`. Run **Login Admin** first."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"Submission was reviewed\", () => {",
									"  pm.expect(json.data.status).to.be.oneOf([\"APPROVED\", \"REJECTED\"]);",
									"  pm.expect(json.data.reviewerId).to.be.a(\"string\");",
									"  pm.expect(json.data.reviewedAt).to.be.a(\"string\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"auth": {
						"type": "bearer",
						"bearer": [
							{
								"key": "token",
								"value": "{{adminAccessToken}}",
								"type": "string"
							}
						]
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Delete Submission",
					"request": {
						"method": "DELETE",
						"header": [],
